2.3 Project Goal
To establish a sustainable and profitable climate-smart indigenous chicken broiler enterprise that improves meat production, enhances students' practical agricultural skills, and demonstrates modern poultry management practices.
2.4 Specific Objectives
The project sought to:
1.	Construct a climate-smart poultry house.
2.	Rear sixty (60) improved Kienyeji broiler chicks to market weight.
3.	Reduce mortality through proper health management.
4.	Improve feed utilization and reduce wastage.
5.	Maintain accurate production and financial records.
6.	Market quality chicken meat competitively.
7.	Promote value addition and environmental conservation.
8.	Evaluate the profitability of the enterprise.
